---
 CMakeLists.txt                                     | 2 +-
 README.md                                          | 2 +-
 rfnoc/fpga/oot-blocks/rfnoc_block_aurora/README.md | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 59c5f91..a2070f3 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ endif()
 ###########################################################################
 # Find UHD
 ###########################################################################
-find_package(UHD 4.9)
+find_package(UHD 4.10)
 if(UHD_FOUND)
     message(STATUS "Found UHD:")
     message(STATUS " * Version: ${UHD_VERSION}")
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 10c6c09..84edd0f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ ________________________________________________________________________________
 
 ## Updated build for X310 Aurora OOT block
 
-This build is using uhd 4.9.0.1 and the isntructions to build this Aurora image for X310 are as follows:
+This build is using uhd 4.10.0.0 and the isntructions to build this Aurora image for X310 are as follows:
 
 Build and install UHD from the modified source to get the updated BSP files:                                                                                                                                       
   cd /home/yuriy/test/uhd/host                              
diff --git a/rfnoc/fpga/oot-blocks/rfnoc_block_aurora/README.md b/rfnoc/fpga/oot-blocks/rfnoc_block_aurora/README.md
index bd048d4..783112f 100644
--- a/rfnoc/fpga/oot-blocks/rfnoc_block_aurora/README.md
+++ b/rfnoc/fpga/oot-blocks/rfnoc_block_aurora/README.md
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ For more detailed information on the Aurora RFNoC block, please refer to the ful
 > implementation on the remote compute node, which may require additional HDL expertise.
 
 ### Pre-requisites
-- **UHD Version**: Install UHD version 4.9 or later.
+- **UHD Version**: Install UHD version 4.10 or later.
 - **FPGA Image**: The Aurora RFNoC block needs to be included in the FPGA image.
   You can use the `rfnoc_image_builder` to build FPGA images from the following image core
